Database schema history
=======================

Alembic applies the ordered revisions in versions/. Keep historical revisions:
fresh installations and older databases need the full upgrade chain. They are
not unused application code.

The migration environment imports app.models to populate SQLModel metadata and
uses the synchronous database URI from app.core.config. Request handlers use the
separate asynchronous engine. Production startup runs `alembic upgrade head`
after its database becomes reachable.

Inspect the local Docker database from the repository root:

    docker compose run --rm api alembic -c /app/alembic.ini current
    docker compose run --rm api alembic -c /app/alembic.ini history

For an approved schema change, generate a revision, review its SQL and implement
the downgrade. Verify upgrade and downgrade against a disposable local database
before release. Autogeneration cannot decide whether a data migration is safe.

The regular test suite recreates its own careerhub_test schema. Passing it does
not prove that an existing production database can migrate successfully.
